 "root_cause": "The ASR decoder retained all decoded PCM without checking the actual output sample count; compressed download size and source duration metadata do not bound decoded input. The normal resampling path also never flushed its delayed output, dropping tail samples at8/44.1/48kHz in the real native controls.",
 "contract": {
  "sample_rate_hz": 16000,
  "channels": 1,
  "max_duration_s": 7200,
  "max_samples": 115200000,
  "max_accumulated_s16_pcm_bytes": 230400000,
  "max_returned_float32_bytes": 460800000,
  "error_code": "media_audio_duration_out_of_range",
  "job_state": "failed",
  "model_construction_order_unchanged": true,
  "asr_inference_started_on_over_budget_input": false,
  "partial_transcript_published": false
 },
 "changes": [
  "Check accumulated16kHz mono output samples before reading each PCM plane, including delayed tail frames",
  "Flush the resampler at normal EOF, tolerate passthrough None tail items, retain exact samples*2 plane length",
  "Close input container and PCM buffer on normal and exceptional exits; copy once to owned float32 then normalize in place",
  "Map the new precise input error through the existing MediaProcessor and durable failed-job path; no automatic retry"
 ],
 "limits": [
  "The accumulated s16 PCM is capped at230400000 bytes, and the returned float32 array at115200000 elements",
  "This is not a measurement or proof of total peak memory, codec/resampler internals, one native frame, model allocation or old system commit/native failures",
  "Model construction remains before decoding; oversize inputs prevent transcribe inference, not initial local model construction",
  "The existing900-second host cancellation/termination budget is unchanged",
  "The previous4000-row/24000-character ASR output budget remains; infinite empty ASR streams are unchanged",
  "The actual7200-second large allocation was not exercised; native small exact/one-sample-over cases and a production-domain constant agreement cover the bound",
  "No conclusion about the allocation owner or causes of historical native exits, UI failures or system commit exhaustion"
 ],
